{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SptSVYSCxCqq1ge8s31h1h","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ACGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"},{\"title\":\"Are numerical scores important for grant assessment? A cross-sectional study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11362741/\"},{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"Ranking versus rating in peer review of research grant applications\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10553257/\"},{\"title\":\"Peer Review of Grant Applications: Criteria Used and Qualitative Study of Reviewer Practices\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3460995/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about ICLR review processes from the 2024-2025 conference cycle, but specific ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines were not found in these results. \n\nThe most relevant result I found was from the ICLR 2024-2025 corpus, which indicates that most review scores remained unchanged (2024: 81%, 2025: 75%), followed by increases (2024: 17%, 2025: 23%), with decreases being the least frequent outcome (2024: 1%, 2025: 1%) after the rebuttal process.\n\nAdditionally, according to ICLR Area Chair Guidelines, ICLR does not plan to share the rating curve, with the goal being to accept quality papers and not be constrained to curve fitting.\n\nHowever, the specific ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and rating scale details don't appear to be publicly available yet through this search. Since ICLR 2027 is still in the future, the official guidelines may not have been released. You may want to check the official ICLR website (iclr.cc) directly when the call for papers is announced for that year.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b56c3912-c718-44fa-8fad-b4f0c1958f5c","uuid":"9003de58-9522-495e-abbb-3a3987d62412","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:29:37.229Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Rdk1LEsdjieqv34AyEo9GY","content":[{"title":"Area Chair Guidelines","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ACGuide"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"},{"title":"Are numerical scores important for grant assessment? A cross-sectional study","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11362741/"},{"title":"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462"},{"title":"Ranking versus rating in peer review of research grant applications","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10553257/"},{"title":"Peer Review of Grant Applications: Criteria Used and Qualitative Study of Reviewer Practices","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3460995/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about ICLR review processes from the 2024-2025 conference cycle, but specific ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines were not found in these results. \n\nThe most relevant result I found was from the ICLR 2024-2025 corpus, which indicates that most review scores remained unchanged (2024: 81%, 2025: 75%), followed by increases (2024: 17%, 2025: 23%), with decreases being the least frequent outcome (2024: 1%, 2025: 1%) after the rebuttal process.\n\nAdditionally, according to ICLR Area Chair Guidelines, ICLR does not plan to share the rating curve, with the goal being to accept quality papers and not be constrained to curve fitting.\n\nHowever, the specific ICLR 2027 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and rating scale details don't appear to be publicly available yet through this search. Since ICLR 2027 is still in the future, the official guidelines may not have been released. You may want to check the official ICLR website (iclr.cc) directly when the call for papers is announced for that year."],"durationSeconds":6.231949958000001}}
